# scenarios/6_salaries.books: loaded by ledger_server into 6_salaries.db the first time it is picked,
# and again by Start over. Amounts are in cents.
title	6. Salaries: what an employee costs, and who gets it
about	A salary costs the company more than the employee receives. On a gross salary of 4,000 the company adds its own social security (here 25%, 1,000), so the employee costs 5,000. The employee's own social security (13.07%, 522.80) and the withholding tax (900) are kept back from the gross: 2,577.20 is paid out.
about	What is kept back is not the company's: like VAT, it is collected for others and owed (Social security due, Withholding tax due) until paid to the social security office (ONSS/RSZ) and the tax office. Only Payroll and Employer social security are costs.
currency	USD
account	100000	equity	Capital
account	550000	asset	Bank account
account	400001	asset	Customer 1
account	453000	liability	Withholding tax due
account	454000	liability	Social security due
account	455000	liability	Salaries due
account	700000	revenue	Sales
account	620000	expense	Payroll
account	621000	expense	Employer social security
